# 380 — D-137: review of raw evidence vs published conclusions (logs 366–376, SECURITY.md D-136, R178..R184 plan)
# method: recomputation from the raw JSON/k6 summaries already in docs/audit/M8/logs/raw (no re-measurement); code reading
# 2026-11-07. Corrections are FORWARD (old logs are not edited — no-delete/no-rewrite rule).

F1  SECURITY.md (D-136) overstated the on-disk exposure of SEC-09.
    - The master key file + encrypted secrets DB exist ONLY if AGOS_SECRETS_DB is set; render.yaml does not set it.
    - The PIN fingerprint key file is ALWAYS created (TMPDIR) unless AGOS_PIN_FINGERPRINT_KEY is set; render.yaml does not set it.
    - Render Free FS is ephemeral (https://render.com/docs/free): such files are regenerated on restart/spin-down, but any
      provider credential decrypted or copied while a vulnerable build was live stays valid until rotated at the provider.
    -> correction: SECURITY.md §SEC-09 D-137; runbook docs/audit/M8/prep/SEC09_EXPOSURE_RUNBOOK.md.

F2  Log 368 summary table reports k6's INTERPOLATED p95, while the declared method is nearest-rank on raw samples.
      volatile_normal   api-sse   table 21.159 ms  raw nearest-rank 46.531 ms
      live-local_base   api-auth  table 42.649 ms  raw nearest-rank 90.871 ms
      live-local_base   api-sse   table 69.873 ms  raw nearest-rank 85.219 ms
    No SLO verdict changes (max raw/SLO ratio 0.454). The numbers in the table are not the declared statistic.

F3  Dropped iterations are not reported in the log 368 table:
      live-local_baseline api-auth 6 ; live-local_normal api-health 3 ; fr_storage_sec10 3.
    The open-model rate was therefore not fully delivered; small, but must be shown next to every throughput figure.

F4  live-local_baseline api-auth tail: p99 1436 ms (raw nearest-rank 1486.9 ms), max 1732.8 ms against a p95 of ~91 ms.
    No p99 SLO exists for auth, so no verdict — but the tail was never discussed. Cause not investigated (shared 2-CPU
    sandbox with generator co-located is the leading, UNVERIFIED hypothesis). R-177 on separated nodes must report it.

